<title>USA: K.C. Southern, partner bid for Mexican rail line.</title>
<headline>K.C. Southern, partner bid for Mexican rail line.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kansas City Southern Industries Inc said Monday it and its Mexican partner, Transportacion Maritima SA de CV , submitted a bid for the northeast railroad line in Mexico known as Line  no. 1.</p>
<p>The bid was made as part of the privatization process for Mexico's railroad.</p>
<p>The Mexican government is expected to open bids on December 5, Kansas City Southern said.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
